(Abstract) Tj
T*
(Background: Hypertension is increasingly prevalent in sub-Saharan Africa, yet rural) Tj
T*
(populations face substantial barriers to clinic-based care including distance,) Tj
T*
(transportation costs, and limited facility capacity. Community health worker) Tj
T*
(\(CHW\)-coordinated remote consultation with clinicians represents a potential strategy to) Tj
T*
(extend care access while maintaining quality. Methods: The SEARCH Sapphire study is a) Tj
T*
(mixed-methods implementation trial in rural western Kenya and southwestern Uganda. Adults) Tj
T*
(aged >=40 years with moderate-severe hypertension will be randomized to CHW-facilitated) Tj
T*
(remote clinical consultation \(intervention\) or usual clinic-based care \(control\). The) Tj
T*
(trial incorporates both quantitative measurement of blood pressure control and health) Tj
T*
(system outcomes, and qualitative exploration of acceptability through in-depth interviews) Tj
T*
(with patients \(n~40\) and healthcare providers \(n~15\). Qualitative data will examine) Tj
T*
(perceived quality, accessibility, integration into existing workflows, and) Tj
T*
(barriers/facilitators to implementation. Mixed-methods integration will assess whether) Tj
T*
(CHW-remote models are effective, acceptable, and sustainable for rural hypertension) Tj
T*
(management.) Tj
